  "constitutionalAuthorityStatementText": "<pre>\n[Congressional Record Volume 166, Number 100 (Thursday, May 28, 2020)]\n[House]\nFrom the Congressional Record Online through the Government Publishing Office [<a href=\"https://www.gpo.gov\">www.gpo.gov</a>]\nBy Mr. DAVID P. ROE of Tennessee:\nH.R. 7059.\nCongress has the power to enact this legislation pursuant\nto the following:\nArticle I, Section 8 of the United States Constitution,\nwhich states ``[t]he Congress shall have power to lay and\ncollect taxes, duties, imposts and excises, to pay the debts\nand provide for the common defense and general welfare of the\nUnited States; but all duties, imposts and excises shall be\nuniform throughout the United States.''\n[Page H2359]\n</pre>",
